{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added `y_safestan_copy`, a deterministic copy of `y`, because the original model computes the moving-average residual recursion in `transformed parameters` using `y` before the likelihood statement. SafeStan protected data cannot be referenced before being observed, nor in transformed blocks. The recursion now uses `y_safestan_copy` as a context input, while the protected variable `y` is scored exactly once with the original built-in normal likelihood. The added data field satisfies `y_safestan_copy = y` elementwise.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> Q; // num previous noise terms
  int<lower=3> T; // num observations
  vector[T] y; // observation at time t
  vector[T] y_safestan_copy; // deterministic copy of y for pre-observation MA recursion
}
parameters {
  real mu; // mean
  real<lower=0> sigma; // error scale
  vector[2] theta; // error coeff, lag -t
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[T] epsilon; // error term at time t
  for (t in 1 : T) {
    epsilon[t] = y_safestan_copy[t] - mu;
    for (q in 1 : min(t - 1, Q)) {
      epsilon[t] = epsilon[t] - theta[q] * epsilon[t - q];
    }
  }
}
model {
  vector[T] eta;
  mu ~ cauchy(0, 2.5);
  theta ~ cauchy(0, 2.5);
  sigma ~ cauchy(0, 2.5);
  for (t in 1 : T) {
    eta[t] = mu;
    for (q in 1 : min(t - 1, Q)) {
      eta[t] = eta[t] + theta[q] * epsilon[t - q];
    }
  }
  y ~ normal(eta, sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"Q":1,"T":6,"y":[3.4298418875568037,3.2828066162435148,6.929902029995733,3.7566920884257873,2.0422900454555952,6.761627777291836],"y_safestan_copy":[3.4298418875568037,3.2828066162435148,6.929902029995733,3.7566920884257873,2.0422900454555952,6.761627777291836]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
